WEBVTT

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:08.470
As we cast our eyes above to the boundless sky, we know

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:16.570
Whatever tomorrow brings, the sun will always shine

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:20.610
So won't you come with me?

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.710
It's almost time for the school bell to ring

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.880
And every moment by moment

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.340
I feel more and more like I could fly

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.800
This feeling fills my thoughts and sets my heart alight

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:49.220
It's this moment I love most of all

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:53.890
In my bag I hold all the things I've overcome

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:57.650
And on their wings, I'll fly into the future

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:02.190
We can do anything, at any time and any place

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.660
And no one can stop us even if they try

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:10.290
From ING and that alone can we proceed

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:14.210
Carrying all our feelings as we go

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:18.210
Flying with our dreams for all to see

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:24.680
Let's close today's chapter, and start a new page!

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:40.900
Sixteen-chan, are you doing some more maintenance?

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.530
You haven't fired enough to need cleaning again.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.900
It seems obvious to be extra careful at a time like this.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.820
If you're doing all that, why not just bring along—

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.950
I don't need that dud.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:51.660
If she were here, she'd just cause more trouble.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.200
Sixteen-chan...

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.970
You know, field stripping

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:07.880
makes it sound like you're stripping naked outside.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.180
Get outta here!

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.850
Where's the event area?!

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:25.690
It's finally time for the semis.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.700
I guess Elle-chan isn't coming...

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.040
She'll be here!

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.750
She'll definitely show up!

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.500
She always has in the past!

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.250
She always...

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.360
... breaks!

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.420
... needs repairing!

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.000
... gets sent back to the manufacturer...

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.920
I've never seen her actually make it...

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:49.890
Why isn't Elle-chan coming?

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.760
If they fought alongside each other,

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.600
I'm sure Sixteen-chan would understand Elle-chan better.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:59.060
The next team is their fated matchup.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.190
The pair of the T91, made in Taiwan,

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:04.230
and the Steyr AUG, made in Austria.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:08.780
The T91 was designed with the M16 as a reference point,

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:13.240
and the AUG is the world's most successful bullpup rifle.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:17.040
Oh, Sixteen-chan is an improved successor and Elle-chan's rival.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.330
She's not an improved version.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.120
She's a cheap ripoff.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.710
Sixteen-chan...

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.510
I'm not losing to a copycat.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:31.180
I'll show her just how strong the real thing is.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:33.430
Come on. Let me have some too.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:35.350
We all use the same NATO rounds, after all—

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:40.890
Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:44.650
Funko-chan messed up making those, so she pushed them out of the way.

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:47.150
I put in chili pepper instead of paprika.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:49.440
They're both powders and have the same color, you know?

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.780
It takes a second for it to kick in.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:53.280
That didn't take a second at all!

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.620
Don't just let me eat weird things like that!

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.490
I'm delicate!

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:57.870
You're a barricade?

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.330
I don't need any lame puns from you!

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:00.870
I get enough of those from Fourteen-oneechan.

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:04.210
Did you catch a cold?

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.670
Someone's talking about me.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.000
Could be.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.760
I doubt they're saying anything nice, though.

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.410
Well, I'm sure they can't help it. I <i>am</i> pretty hot.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:14.680
True. You're the "God, not again" cutie.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:17.760
Anyway, Fal, how's the tournament going?

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.390
It might get a little tricky for them.

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:20.680
Let me see.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.190
Oh, that's bad.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:27.150
They're in the village arena which is littered with huts.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:30.030
The visibility's a lot higher than in the jungle.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:34.950
And the flags are in each team's camp, hidden behind large trees.

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:36.780
You won't be able to get a direct shot,

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.290
so you'll need to advance deep into enemy territory.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.460
There's nowhere to hide out there,

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:48.420
so it'll be difficult to attack without backup.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:51.210
But won't it be easy if she focuses on defense?

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:56.600
She's up against the T91 with the telescopic stock

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:00.310
and the Steyr AUG with its interchangeable barrels.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:05.100
It can either be set up for jungle warfare, or it can be used in the city. It's pretty powerful.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.970
It'd be hard to block all their attacks.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.070
<i>First match of the semifinals.</i>

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:17.490
<i>Team Echo vs. Team Golf.</i>

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:18.700
<i>Begin!</i>

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.640
I can't get anywhere like this.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:00.780
Damn it.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:07.290
When one of them advances, the other provides covering fire.

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:10.420
Then the person who was advancing lays down covering fire,

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:12.420
and the other one advances.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:14.340
A textbook tactical maneuver.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:18.390
It'll be pretty hard for Sixteen to handle this by herself.

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.680
Elle-chan...

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:24.470
If you set your watch so that the hour hand points toward the sun,

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:28.440
the halfway mark between 12 and the sun points south.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.060
Elle, I know which way we're heading.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.610
Although I dunno where we are, so it's kinda pointless.

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:36.440
But don't worry,

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:39.490
I'll definitely get you to the tournament.

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:41.070
Let's go, Elle.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.710
They're getting cocky because I'm out here on my own.

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:57.050
If Elle were here...

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.560
If she were here, she'd just cause more problems!

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.310
I don't need that dud!

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:14.730
In that case...

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:22.780
If I fire off to the right,

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:25.870
the one on the left can't see me to lay down covering fire.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:28.250
First I need to focus on the enemy advancing from the right.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.720
This is it!

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:54.810
How did this happen?!

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:56.900
I've been cleaning it thoroughly...

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:01.320
Ugh... my stomach...

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:02.200
Wait!

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:04.280
It was those chicken nuggets, wasn't it?

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:05.910
Yeah, the chicken nuggets.

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:10.290
The Ljungman system used for the operation of the M16

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:12.960
causes the mechanics to accumulate muck

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.880
when poor quality powder is used.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:16.040
During the Vietnam War,

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:18.130
they used different powder than the one specified,

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.760
causing frequent problems with the gun.

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:29.640
Damn Fukko, making me eat that thing!

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.850
I told her I was delicate!

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.310
It jammed again.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:41.240
I'm not supposed to be a bolt action rifle.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:42.130
What am I supposed to do now?!

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:47.030
They know I can't shoot continuously, so they're closing in...

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:49.410
What should I do?

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:55.380
This is bad. They're already pretty close.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:57.090
If they both jump me,

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.800
I won't win with my gun like this.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.510
What a dud! And right when I need it!

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:04.510
<i>All you do is break.</i>

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.470
<i>You're a dud.</i>

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:10.020
Oh yeah...

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:12.680
A dud...

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:17.810
Elle doesn't understand me.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:21.650
I'll show you how I fight.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.350
<i>We both attack her position simultaneously.</i>

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:30.790
<i>Roger that.</i>

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:31.750
<i>Ready...</i>

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:32.750
<i>Go!</i>

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:05.900
<i>Winner: Team Echo!</i>

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:07.610
What was that?

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.910
She was fanning.

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:11.410
Fanning?

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:14.250
It's something you do when you want to fire multiple rounds from a revolver.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:15.620
That's what she was doing?!

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:20.670
So she used a Western technique instead of something for an assault rifle.

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:23.300
Huh? I wonder what's going on.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:28.470
How embarrassing.

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:30.410
I wonder if it got blown away by the wind.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:31.550
There it is!

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:33.470
That's it, right?

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:37.690
That's a G-string, isn't it?

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:39.930
You adjust the length using the string...

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:53.370
You're in the final now.

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:55.500
That was close.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.670
It wasn't close at all.

00:10:57.670 --> 00:10:59.250
It was easy.

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:03.880
If you two win your next match, we'll be facing each other in the final.

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:05.710
I won't hold back.

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:08.550
Look who's acting like she's already won.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:10.590
Sako...

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:12.600
Our team is going to win.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:17.520
We're gonna take you down in the final, Sixteen-han.

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:18.850
What'd you say?!

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:20.310
I don't think so!

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:22.190
We'll take you out before you even get there.

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:25.110
Sounds like this'll be fun.

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:27.070
See you on the field.

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:28.360
What was that about?

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:29.950
They annoy the hell outta me.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:37.750
Elle!

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.590
Watch out for potholes.

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:47.340
You're heavy, y'know.

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:49.630
I can't.

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:53.640
I can't... I won't be of any use even if I do turn up.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:54.890
Elle...

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:57.080
No.

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:59.430
I'm taking you there, even if I have to carry you.

00:11:59.430 --> 00:12:00.230
But...

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:03.710
You and Sixteen have to fight together.

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:06.480
Elle, do you hate Sixteen?

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:09.940
I think so...

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:11.150
Really?

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:14.120
Maybe.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.580
Do you <i>really</i>?

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:22.080
I guess I like her.

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:25.040
Then let's get a move on, Elle.

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:27.250
Okay.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:33.550
This combat area has a big lake in the center

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:35.760
with a bridge running across it.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:37.390
You can see people on the bridge pretty well,

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:39.430
so you'll be a sitting duck.

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:43.140
But that means that we'll be able to provide cover from a wider area.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:44.730
If one of us takes the bridge

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:47.270
and the other takes the shore, we can head for the flag

00:12:47.270 --> 00:12:49.320
while covering each other.

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:50.860
In the worst case scenario,

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:54.410
the enemy moves as a single unit along the opposite shore toward our flag.

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:56.530
We'll worry about that if it happens.

00:12:56.530 --> 00:12:58.240
We can't both attack,

00:12:58.240 --> 00:13:01.290
so it'll just be a case of whoever gets to the flag first, wins.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:03.850
<i>But why...</i>

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:08.250
<i>Why do they care so much about Sixteen-chan?</i>

00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:12.670
<i>Second match of the semifinals.</i>

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:15.720
<i>Team Delta vs. Team Foxtrot.</i>

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:16.930
<i>Begin!</i>

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:28.690
I ran straight into them! The enemy's over here!

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.770
<i>I'll cover from here.</i>

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:42.290
<i>Advance with caution.</i>

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:44.810
<i>Go!</i>

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:50.610
<i>Where's her teammate?</i>

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:51.840
<i>Is she defending further down?</i>

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:53.840
<i>Or is she still on the other side of the bridge?</i>

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:55.840
<i>Now, come out!</i>

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:07.150
Eighteen-chan!

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:14.280
She was on the other shore?!

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:16.130
She wasn't planning on helping out her teammate at all?

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:21.370
The bridge is in the way!

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:25.040
At this rate, our flag will...

00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:26.420
What should I do?

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:28.310
What should I do?

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:33.460
There!

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:49.150
I think... I got her.

00:14:52.690 --> 00:14:53.980
They ricocheted?

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:57.530
She bounced the shots off the water and made them go under the bridge.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:09.710
That was nice, my little bunny.

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:12.340
That was truly wonderful.

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:16.050
So you want me to tease you and play with you?

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:17.800
Of course you do.

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:22.100
Look at what you did to me...

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:24.570
You're mine.

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:27.310
My cute, adorable, little bunny rabbit.

00:15:35.690 --> 00:15:38.630
Now, time to go hunting.

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:41.360
Funko-chan!

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:46.660
I'm fine!

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:48.790
She can't hit me here!

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:51.000
We'll see about that.

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:53.540
She just doesn't learn.

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:56.710
What's that?

00:15:56.710 --> 00:15:58.260
Metal fragments?

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:05.930
My eye!

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:08.140
Ouch...

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:12.690
Haven't you heard of fragmentation before?

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:16.970
My little bunny.

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:19.460
I'm not your bunny!

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:27.620
You're supposed to wait until I'm done talking.

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:31.820
Funko-chan!

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:37.460
You see, fragmentation is when a round shatters.

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:44.640
The low-caliber high-velocity rounds we use rotate over 300,000 times a minute.

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:46.350
With poor quality bullets,

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:50.470
the jackets can separate from the cores during flight.

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:55.480
You can imagine what would happen if they hit the bark of a tree.

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:58.940
You're in no condition to fight with your eye like that.

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:05.530
Next I get to smash Sixteen's nose in, since she's been acting all high and mighty.

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:08.700
That scrap metal companion of hers is tired of putting up with her.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:10.410
Her friends have all abandoned her.

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:14.620
Sixteen-han's era is about to come to an end.

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:16.130
That's not true!

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:19.050
We all care about each other!

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:22.300
Elle-chan loves Sixteen-chan!

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:25.010
Sixteen-chan cares about her—

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:31.770
Funko-chan!

00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:34.210
<i>Winner: Team Delta!</i>

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:39.770
Stop! The match is over!

00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:41.780
I didn't hear anything.

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:47.240
I couldn't hear the match-ending signal over my gunshots.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:54.580
Elle-chan... will be here.

00:17:57.330 --> 00:17:59.040
What are you doing?! Stop it!

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:04.970
E-Everyone will...

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.260
Such a sweet sound...

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:13.020
I think I'm going to come.

00:18:18.400 --> 00:18:19.730
Stop it!

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:26.400
It's against the rules for someone who's been gunned down to continue participating in the game.

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:28.030
Get away from Funko-chan!

00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:30.490
Everyone...

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:34.850
I think you should go play with someone else who's already out.

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:53.350
Sniping with rapid fire from over 300 meters outside the boundary...

00:18:53.810 --> 00:18:56.640
The only one who could pull off a feat like that is...

00:18:56.640 --> 00:19:00.310
G3-senpai's special technique came in handy, don't you think, Elle?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:05.230
Elle...-chan

00:19:06.110 --> 00:19:07.030
Up we go.

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:12.330
Thanks.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:13.580
My name's Galil.

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:14.790
What's your name?

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:16.910
Eighteen...

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:18.790
You fought me without even knowing that?

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:19.710
Yep!

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:24.840
How's Fukko?

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:26.960
They said her receiver's a bit dented,

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:29.130
but other than that, she should still be operational.

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:31.680
They're fighting dirty!

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:33.760
I'll get revenge for her.

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:37.220
Oh yeah, Sig-chan, aren't you going to fight in the match?

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:41.440
My partner Cal-san isn't participating, so I'm just watching.

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:43.480
You don't need a partner.

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:44.980
I mean, look at me.

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:47.400
I'm in the final all by myself.

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:49.450
I never needed a partner.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.320
Sixteen....

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:52.660
Wh-What?

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:55.410
Your thinking is too soft. You're soft serve.

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:58.620
You don't know what kind of tricks Sako's going to pull.

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:01.460
It'd be better for you if you at least had someone else on your side.

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:03.380
Wh-What?

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:05.460
You're not even participating, are you?

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:08.050
If Sako wins, she won't just be someone else's problem anymore.

00:20:08.050 --> 00:20:08.960
Why?

00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:14.930
It's likely that her goal is to take over this school.

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:20.120
<i>It's time for the final!</i>

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:23.500
<i>The match will be contested by Team Delta and Team Echo.</i>

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:26.750
<i>The final will be held in the wetlands area!</i>

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:28.690
<i>Begin!</i>

00:20:34.070 --> 00:20:36.410
This isn't the wetlands, this is a swamp.

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:39.250
You should take a detour and head for the grasslands, Elle.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:41.500
You'll sink with your weight.

00:20:45.170 --> 00:20:47.130
Do whatever you want.

00:20:47.130 --> 00:20:49.460
Take point for me while you're at it.

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:51.380
How's it looking?

00:20:52.090 --> 00:20:53.380
Funko-chan!

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:54.890
Are you okay?

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:56.470
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:10.540
<i>She changed her movements to match up with Elle-chan's?</i>

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:11.880
<i>She knows what they're up to?</i>

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:16.320
<i>How could that be?</i>

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:19.790
Look over there.

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:20.370
What is it?

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:21.410
See?

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:23.250
Oh, you're right.

00:21:29.590 --> 00:21:31.800
You're spying for Sako, aren't you?

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:33.590
Shame on you!

00:21:33.590 --> 00:21:35.110
I'm not the type of girl who forgets

00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:37.550
when someone does something for me.

00:21:37.550 --> 00:21:39.600
But more importantly...

00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:43.600
I'm not the type to forget when someone humiliates me.

00:21:55.030 --> 00:21:59.030
Sig-chan!

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:08.210
Let's tear another page off our calendar

00:22:09.210 --> 00:22:15.720
Together we braved

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:27.690
past ages and never-ending conflict

00:22:27.940 --> 00:22:35.280
Together we laughed and cried in those hectic times

00:22:36.150 --> 00:22:40.910
When I ran

00:22:43.830 --> 00:22:54.300
I put my footsteps into the ground

00:22:55.380 --> 00:23:02.050
Let's tear another page off our calendar

00:23:03.010 --> 00:23:09.230
Something is bound to change

00:23:10.600 --> 00:23:17.360
One by one the days I tore off pile up

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:21.280
like a past I cannot erase

00:23:21.740 --> 00:23:27.450
They will be my strength for days to come

00:23:32.130 --> 00:23:34.650
I may seem weak, but when I have to do something,

00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:36.940
I get it done! So don't complain!

00:23:36.940 --> 00:23:37.880
But, who am I?

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:39.150
Next time: Take it!

00:23:39.150 --> 00:23:39.740
Hurry!

00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:40.650
Do it!
